In file mode a UTF-16 file (with an `FF FE` byte order mark) is reported as looking like a binary or UTF-16 file, from its NUL bytes, and outln exits 1, while the other file argument is still outlined.
== args
input/utf16.md
input/ok.md
== file input/utf16.md escaped
\xff\xfec\x00o\x00n\x00s\x00t\x00 \x00a\x00 \x00=\x00 \x001\x00;\x00\
== file input/ok.md
# ok
== stdout
input/ok.md (1 line)
[L1-L1] # ok
== stderr
File input/utf16.md looks like a binary or UTF-16 file, not UTF-8 text
== exit 1
